  "description": "The crawler behind Audisto, a German SaaS platform for technical website analysis and continuous website monitoring. It fetches the accessible URLs of a site so the product can report crawling and indexation errors, hreflang and canonical problems, and internal link-graph issues. The operator runs two crawlers: an Essential crawler that may crawl any site, and a Full crawler that only crawls sites whose ownership has been verified. The bot reference documents automated overload protection — after 10 error responses within a hundred requests the crawler lengthens its delay and reduces parallelism, and relaxes again once the error rate drops below 5 percent — plus a 30-second total request budget and per-content-type response size caps.",
